/**
 * Schema for the execute tool — runs JavaScript in a sandbox with figma.* API.
 */
export const executeSchema = {
    name: 'execute',
    description: `Execute JavaScript code in a sandbox with access to the figma.* API.
Use this to batch multiple operations in a single call (create UIs, modify nodes, read data).
Works in both Figma Design and FigJam files — use \`figma.getEditorType()\` to detect which.

## REQUIRED: Visual Verification Workflow

You MUST follow this workflow when creating or modifying visual elements. You are working blind — you cannot see what you create. Skipping verification leads to broken layouts, overlapping text, misaligned shapes, and unusable components.

1. **Create** a component, section, or page element.
2. **Verify** by calling \`capture_screenshot\` on the created node immediately after.
3. **Inspect** the screenshot for: overlapping text, misaligned elements, missing content, wrong colors, broken shapes, elements extending outside their parent.
4. **Fix** any issues found before moving on to the next element.
5. **Repeat** for each logical group (e.g., each component, each page section, each form).

Do NOT batch-create an entire page and only screenshot at the end. Verify after each meaningful unit so errors don't compound.

## Design Rules
IMPORTANT: When recreating existing app screens in Figma, call the get_design_rules tool first.
It explains how to read CSS from the codebase and translate it accurately to Figma, one element at a time.

## Quick API Reference

**Create (Figma Design):** figma.create(opts) [unified with recursive children], figma.createFrame, figma.createRectangle, figma.createEllipse, figma.createLine, figma.createText, figma.createPolygon, figma.createStar, figma.createVector, figma.createInstance, figma.cloneNode, figma.createPage
**Create (FigJam):** figma.createSection, figma.createSticky, figma.createShape, figma.createConnector — also available via figma.create({ type: "section" | "sticky" | "shape" | "connector" })
**Read:** figma.getNode, figma.getSelection(), figma.getCurrentPage, figma.getPages, figma.getStyles, figma.getLocalComponents, figma.getVariables, figma.searchNodes, figma.captureScreenshot, figma.getEditorType(), figma.listFonts, figma.scrollAndZoomIntoView
**Update:** figma.updateNode, figma.moveNode, figma.swapComponent, figma.setCurrentPage
**Operations:** figma.group, figma.ungroup, figma.flatten, figma.booleanOperation, figma.detachInstance, figma.removeOverrides
**Delete:** figma.deleteNode
**Tokens:** figma.createToken(opts), figma.bindToken(opts)
**Components:** figma.toComponent(opts), figma.createVariants(opts), figma.addComponentProperty(opts), figma.setInstanceOverride(opts), figma.createComponentAndInstances(opts) [compound: create component + stamp instances]
**Styles:** figma.createStyle(opts), figma.applyStyle(opts)
**Accessibility:** figma.checkAccessibility(opts)

All methods are async — use \`await\`. Use \`return\` to send results back.
Use \`console.log()\` for debug output (captured in response).
Use \`search_tools\` to discover full parameter details for any method (try category "figjam").

**Colors** must be {r, g, b, a?} objects with values in the 0-1 range. Example: \`{ r: 1, g: 0, b: 0 }\` for red.
**Fills/Strokes** can also be set as Figma-native Paint[] arrays via \`fills\`/\`strokes\` params for gradients and image fills.
**Effects** must be Figma-native Effect[] arrays (e.g., DropShadowEffect, BlurEffect).
**Target specifiers:** use "selection", "name:NodeName", or "page" instead of node IDs.
**Layout:** use raw Figma auto-layout properties: \`layoutMode\`, \`primaryAxisSizingMode\`, \`counterAxisSizingMode\`, \`itemSpacing\`, \`paddingTop/Right/Bottom/Left\`.

## FigJam

In FigJam, use sections (containers), stickies (notes), shapes (diagrams), connectors (lines between nodes), and text. Frames/rectangles are auto-remapped to sections/shapes as a fallback, but prefer explicit FigJam methods.

## Example (Figma Design)

\`\`\`js
const frame = await figma.createFrame({
  name: "Card",
  width: 320, height: 200,
  fillColor: { r: 1, g: 1, b: 1 },
  cornerRadius: 8,
  layoutMode: "VERTICAL",
  primaryAxisSizingMode: "AUTO",
  counterAxisSizingMode: "FIXED",
  itemSpacing: 12,
  paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 16, paddingLeft: 16, paddingRight: 16,
});
await figma.createText({
  text: "Hello World", fontSize: 24, fontWeight: "Bold",
  fillColor: { r: 0, g: 0, b: 0 },
  parentId: frame.id
});
return frame;
\`\`\`

## Example (FigJam)

\`\`\`js
const section = await figma.createSection({ name: "Sprint Planning", width: 800, height: 600 });
const shapeA = await figma.createShape({ text: "Frontend", fillColor: { r: 0.91, g: 0.94, b: 0.996 }, parentId: section.id });
const shapeB = await figma.createShape({ text: "API", x: 400, fillColor: { r: 0.988, g: 0.91, b: 0.902 }, parentId: section.id });
await figma.createConnector({ startNodeId: shapeA.id, endNodeId: shapeB.id, endStrokeCap: "ARROW_EQUILATERAL", text: "REST calls" });
await figma.createSticky({ text: "User story #1", fillColor: { r: 1, g: 0.976, b: 0.694 }, parentId: section.id });
return section;
\`\`\``,
    inputSchema: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
            code: {
                type: 'string',
                description: 'JavaScript code to execute. All figma.* methods are async. Use return to send back results.',
            },
        },
        required: ['code'],
    },
};
